  "description": "Dapper store for DotNetBoost.Auditing, for applications that do not use EF Core. The two\n      tables are the same shape the EF Core store maps — same names, lengths and indexes — so one\n      database serves either. Recording is explicit rather than captured: there is no change\n      tracker to read, so entries are written through IAuditManager and commit with your own work\n      when you hand the store your transaction. SQL written for SQL Server, PostgreSQL and SQLite.",
